    "message": "Formalize prime filtering and its runner reductions as a checked candidate\n\nAdd twelve Lean modules formalizing the finite-choice argument, exact quotient and residue arithmetic, universal prime filtering, actual prime-power units, canonical valuations, partial filtering with full higher-residue preservation, and the distance corollary from Barajas and Serra, The lonely runner with seven runners (2008), Lemma 2 and Corollary 3. Credit the published theorem and track formalization in issue #42.\n\nConnect the arithmetic to actual modular witnesses and the real-time loneliness value. Prime seven needs at most three distinct speeds at each level strictly below the canonical maximum; the highest level is unrestricted. The separate uniform-level theorem needs only a base at least two, with no input-count or primality assumption. The unrestricted six-speed theorem and exceptional dense lower levels remain pending.\n\nThe exact 18-module local gate passed all fresh strict sources, 33 literal contracts, the complete 299-declaration/243-theorem/10-private audit, and all 18 independent stock replays. Require all 68 endpoints and only propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound. Preserve that source/controller snapshot for the public complete gate. This candidate does not alter accepted imports, required registries or result completion statuses; retain all concurrent Li and lattice work.",
    "timestamp": "2026-11-19T18:49:51Z",
